Auto Sync & Self Healing in GitOps

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m exploring one of the most powerful features of GitOps: Auto Sync & Self-Healing 🚀
These features make systems fully automated, reliable, and resilient in production environments.

🔹 Continuous Reconciliation
 GitOps tools continuously monitor:
Desired state (defined in Git)
Actual state (running in the cluster)
They constantly compare both states and ensure the system is always aligned with Git configuration.
This process is called continuous reconciliation.

🔹 Drift Correction (Self-Healing)
 Sometimes the actual system state may change due to:
Manual changes
Failed deployments
Unexpected errors
This creates configuration drift.
GitOps tools automatically detect this drift and:
Revert the system back to the desired state
Apply correct configurations from Git
This behavior is known as self-healing.

🔹 Auto Sync Feature
 With auto-sync enabled:
Any change in Git is automatically deployed
No manual sync required
Faster and consistent updates

💡 Key Insight:
 Auto Sync and Self-Healing ensure that your infrastructure is always correct, consistent, and aligned with Git without manual intervention.
